{"name":"Red Door","hex":"#ac0000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"door","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A portal of entry into a building, room, or vehicle, typically consisting of a rigid plane movable on a hinge. It may have a handle to help open and close, a latch to hold it closed, and a lock that ensures it cannot be opened without a key.","A building with a door, especially a house."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause a collision by opening the door of a vehicle in front of an oncoming cyclist or pedestrian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/door"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Door (venue)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Door was a 2,000 SF event and music space located in the heart of Chelsea, New York City, that remained private to the public for 37 years. Its name changed over the years, but always based on the colors of the front door. The venue attracted a wide array of celebrities and personalities in the music and entertainment world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Door_(venue)","wikidata":"Q23092027"},{"title":"The Red Door (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"The Red Door was a restaurant in Seattle, in the U.S. state of Washington. It was featured on the Food Network's Diners, Drive-Ins and Dives. It closed in 2020."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Red_Door_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q125523226"},{"title":"Door","blocks":[{"text":"A door is a hinged or otherwise movable barrier that allows ingress (entry) into and egress (exit) from an enclosure. The created opening in the wall is a doorway or portal. A door's essential and primary purpose is to provide security by controlling access to the doorway (portal). Conventionally, it is a panel that fits into the doorway of a building, room, or vehicle. Doors are generally made of a material suited to the door's task. They are commonly attached by hinges, but can move by other means, such as slides or counterbalancing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/L-door.png/330px-L-door.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Door","wikidata":"Q36794"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Stone_door.jpg/500px-Stone_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Stone_door.jpg/500px-Stone_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStone_door.jpg"},{"srcset":"htt